      "title": "How the character average and the relevant orbits give termwise vanishing",
      "anchor": "global-word-vanishing",
      "statement": "For distinct words every nonidentity term with geometric Gram label zero is zero. A nonrelevant flag pair has a character ratio −1 on a common unipotent element, forcing its orbital integral to vanish after averaging. The relevant case is WVN-01. Consequently B_uv=0, and the selected squared norm bound for the remaining part gives the full off-diagonal bound.",
